    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a cool start, but I don't want them to look like monsters or aliens—I want them to be humans so the conflict feels more grounded and real. I want the readers to see them as a real, albeit \"savage,\" human culture. How would you describe their physical appearance and skin tones to make them look distinctly different from the fair-skinned, polished people of the Empire? Like, what kind of look would emphasize that they are from these warmer, more unmapped, untamed parts of the world?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
