      "role": "user",
      "content": "The skin tones and cultural markers are great, they really ground the setting. To make the tension even more visceral, I want the readers to feel an almost instinctual sense of danger when these tribes meet the Empire. Since they grew up in such a harsh, untamed environment, how would their temperament or social behaviors naturally differ from the disciplined, intellectual people of the Empire? I'm thinking about how their \"wilder\" nature might manifest in how they interact, approach conflict, or even view things like law and logic compared to the \"enlightened\" protagonists.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
